# Hello World Program in Java

# Basic Code Example
The following is a simple program that displays the message “Hello, World!” on the screen.

##  Code
```java
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");

        // Print/Display to the OutPut Screen/Terminal
        System.out.println("Hello java.......");

        //! (Any Thing Written Inside " " is called String)
        //! (Single Thing Written Inside '' is called Character)

        // Variables/Containers and Data Types
        int age = 25;
        float height = 5.8f;
        char gender = 'M';
        boolean isStudent = true;
        String name = "John";

        // Print/Display variables
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Height: " + height);
        System.out.println("Gender: " + gender);
        System.out.println("Is Student: " + isStudent);

    }
}
    
